mkdir -p ~/k8s-journey/manifests/week4 && cd ~/k8s-journey/manifests/week4


STEP 1: Create ConfigMaps four ways
-----------------------------------
k create cm cm-literal --from-literal=LOG_LEVEL=debug --from-literal=COLOR=blue

cat > app.properties <<EOF
color=green
max_items=50
EOF
k create cm cm-file --from-file=app.properties

cat > app.env <<EOF
DB_HOST=postgres.db.svc.cluster.local
DB_PORT=5432
EOF
k create cm cm-envfile --from-env-file=app.env

k get cm
k describe cm cm-file
k get cm cm-envfile -o yaml

Notice the difference: --from-file makes ONE key (the file name),
--from-env-file makes one key PER LINE.


STEP 2: A ConfigMap in YAML
---------------------------
vi app-config.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: app-config
data:
  LOG_LEVEL: "info"
  GREETING: "Hello from ConfigMap"
  index.html: |
    <h1>Served from a ConfigMap</h1>

k apply -f app-config.yaml


STEP 3: Use it as env vars
--------------------------
vi pod-env.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: env-demo
spec:
  restartPolicy: Never
  containers:
  - name: c
    image: busybox:1.36
    command: ["sh", "-c", "env | sort | grep -E 'LOG_LEVEL|GREETING|DB_|MY_'; sleep 3600"]
    env:
    - name: MY_LEVEL
      valueFrom:
        configMapKeyRef:
          name: app-config
          key: LOG_LEVEL
    - name: MY_NODE
      valueFrom:
        fieldRef:
          fieldPath: spec.nodeName
    envFrom:
    - configMapRef:
        name: cm-envfile
    - configMapRef:
        name: app-config

k apply -f pod-env.yaml
k logs env-demo

Note: "index.html" did not become an env var (invalid name; it is
skipped). Check: k describe pod env-demo | grep -i -A2 warn  /  k get events


STEP 4: Use it as files
-----------------------
vi deploy-web-cm.yaml

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: web-cm
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels: {app: web-cm}
  template:
    metadata:
      labels: {app: web-cm}
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: nginx
        image: nginx:1.27
        volumeMounts:
        - name: html
          mountPath: /usr/share/nginx/html
        - name: props
          mountPath: /etc/app
      volumes:
      - name: html
        configMap:
          name: app-config
          items:
          - key: index.html
            path: index.html
      - name: props
        configMap:
          name: cm-file

k apply -f deploy-web-cm.yaml
POD=$(k get pod -l app=web-cm -o name)
k exec $POD -- ls -la /usr/share/nginx/html
k exec $POD -- cat /etc/app/app.properties
k exec $POD -- curl -s localhost

ls -la shows symlinks (..data -> ..2025_xx). That's how the kubelet
swaps files atomically on update.


STEP 5: Update behaviour
------------------------
Edit app-config.yaml: change the index.html text and LOG_LEVEL to
"warn". Apply.

Mounted file (wait up to ~60-90 s):
  watch -n5 "kubectl exec $POD -- curl -s localhost"
  -> changes without restart

Env var:
  k delete pod env-demo && k apply -f pod-env.yaml && k logs env-demo
  -> new value only because the pod was recreated

For a Deployment using env vars you'd run:
  k rollout restart deploy/<name>


STEP 6: Use your config in your own app
---------------------------------------
cd ~/k8s-journey/myapp
Edit app.py so the message comes from an env var:

  import os
  ...
  msg = os.environ.get("GREETING", "Hello")
  return f"{msg}! Served by container: {socket.gethostname()}\n"

Build and push as v3 (docker or podman). Then:
  k create deploy myapp --image=YOURUSER/myapp:v3
  k set env deploy/myapp --from=configmap/app-config --keys=GREETING
  k port-forward deploy/myapp 5000:5000 &
  curl localhost:5000 ; kill %1

(Note: k set env changes the template, so it triggers a rollout.)


STEP 7: Immutable ConfigMap
---------------------------
k create cm frozen --from-literal=A=1 --dry-run=client -o yaml > frozen.yaml
echo "immutable: true" >> frozen.yaml
k apply -f frozen.yaml
k patch cm frozen -p '{"data":{"A":"2"}}'     # Forbidden


STEP 8: Missing ConfigMap
-------------------------
k run broken-cm --image=busybox:1.36 --overrides='{"spec":{"containers":[{"name":"c","image":"busybox:1.36","command":["sleep","3600"],"envFrom":[{"configMapRef":{"name":"does-not-exist"}}]}]}}'
k get pod broken-cm          # CreateContainerConfigError
k describe pod broken-cm | tail -3
Add "optional: true" under configMapRef to make it non-fatal.


